## Deviation note

The ticket asks to "make the callout right from the trigger." **Synchronous HTTP callouts are not permitted inside a trigger** (platform rule: callouts are only allowed in future/queueable/batch/invocable contexts). The closest equivalent is to enqueue a `Queueable` job from the trigger; the job executes in the very next execution cycle, which for a single-record insert is effectively immediate. I preserve the "one request per new account" requirement: every account gets its own `POST` with a one-element JSON array so the ERP team can trace each record independently.

For the 200-account batch (marketplace), a single transaction may issue at most 100 callouts, so the Queueable processes 100 at a time and chains a second Queueable for the remainder.

